STGR PATCH: 0004 — STGR Gaming Mode and performance preference block
Purpose:                Implement STGR Gaming Mode (browser resource management while
                        gaming) and the performance preference defaults / memory profiles.
                        Gaming Mode suspends background tabs and reduces timers, network,
                        animations and preloading — it never touches other applications,
                        GPU drivers, or the OS.
Files changed:          browser/app/profile/firefox.js
                        browser/components/stgr/gamingmode/moz.build (new)
                        browser/components/stgr/gamingmode/STGRGamingMode.sys.mjs (new)
                        browser/base/content/browser-init.js
Security impact:        None. No security mitigation is disabled. Tabs playing audio/video,
                        downloads, WebRTC calls and the active tab are protected.
Performance impact:     When enabled: reduced background CPU/RAM/network by design.
Upstream compatibility: browser-init.js (_delayedStartup) is the current main-window
                        startup hook (verified on the release branch); rebase risk MEDIUM.
                        Verify the STGRGamingMode import against the pinned Firefox version.
Note:                   DEPENDENCY: must be applied AFTER 0002 — the firefox.js insertion
                        anchors on the "// END STGR PRIVACY PREFS" marker that 0002 injects
                        at the END of firefox.js (series order guarantees this). The injected
                        block is the exact content of
                        stgr/config/preferences/performance.js (enforced by
                        lint_prefs_sync.py / --verify-prefs-sync).

                        IMPORTANT: Firefox 153 no longer ships
                        resource://gre/modules/Services.sys.mjs — Services is a global in
                        the ESM environment (stock modules use it without importing, e.g.
                        AboutNewTabRedirector), and XPCOMUtils no longer has
                        defineLazyGetter (use ChromeUtils.defineLazyGetter instead).
                        DO NOT re-add either; the module below relies on the Services
                        global and imports only modules that exist in the pinned release.

diff --git a/browser/app/profile/firefox.js b/browser/app/profile/firefox.js
--- a/browser/app/profile/firefox.js
+++ b/browser/app/profile/firefox.js
@@ -3736,1 +3736,39 @@
 // END STGR PRIVACY PREFS
+
+// BEGIN STGR PERFORMANCE PREFS
+
+// ---- Default performance posture -----------------------------------
+// Hardware acceleration stays ON (never disabled by default).
+pref("layers.acceleration.force-enabled", true);   // hardware acceleration
+pref("gfx.webrender.all", true);                   // WebRender default path
+// Reduce idle background activity.
+pref("network.http.throttle.enable", true);
+pref("browser.sessionstore.interval", 30000);      // session writes less chatty
+pref("browser.tabs.unloadOnLowMemory", true);      // memory-pressure unloading
+
+// ---- Memory profiles --------------------------------------------------
+// normal:    stock Firefox behavior
+// balanced:  moderate background-tab suspension and timer throttling
+// aggressive: maximum background resource reduction (active tab protected)
+
+pref("stgr.memoryProfile.normal.tabs.suspendAfterSeconds", 0);
+pref("stgr.memoryProfile.balanced.tabs.suspendAfterSeconds", 600);
+pref("stgr.memoryProfile.aggressive.tabs.suspendAfterSeconds", 120);
+pref("stgr.memoryProfile.aggressive.timerThrottling", true);
+pref("stgr.memoryProfile.aggressive.backgroundNetwork", false);
+pref("stgr.memoryProfile.aggressive.animation", false);
+pref("stgr.memoryProfile.aggressive.preload", false);
+
+// ---- Gaming Mode preset (applied when stgr.gamingMode.enabled) --------
+pref("stgr.gamingMode.suspendBackgroundTabs", true);
+pref("stgr.gamingMode.reduceTimers", true);
+pref("stgr.gamingMode.reduceNetwork", true);
+pref("stgr.gamingMode.reduceAnimations", true);
+pref("stgr.gamingMode.pausePreload", true);
+// Protected media (audio/video/calls) and downloads are NEVER unloaded:
+pref("stgr.gamingMode.protect.audio", true);
+pref("stgr.gamingMode.protect.video", true);
+pref("stgr.gamingMode.protect.downloads", true);
+pref("stgr.gamingMode.protect.webrtc", true);
+
+// END STGR PERFORMANCE PREFS
